# Ownership of the perimeter repository.
#
# The split matters: changing WHO is inside the perimeter is a routine, additive act; changing WHAT the
# perimeter protects, or what a shared rule template allows, affects every division at once.

# Default: nothing lands without the perimeter owners.
*                           @your-org/network-team @your-org/security-team

# Baseline — the services under protection, the dry-run window, the attribute budget.
# Both teams, always: this file is the definition of the boundary.
/perimeter/policy.yaml      @your-org/network-team @your-org/security-team

# Rule templates. A change here propagates to every division already using the profile, so it is reviewed
# like a shared library, not like a config tweak.
/perimeter/profiles/        @your-org/network-team @your-org/security-team

# Access levels — the context conditions (corporate network, managed device). Widening an IP range here
# quietly widens every rule that references it.
/perimeter/access-levels/   @your-org/network-team @your-org/security-team

# Which repository may request which projects. A team cannot widen its own list, because the list is not
# in its repository — that property only holds as long as this file needs the same approval as a profile.
/perimeter/contributors.yaml @your-org/network-team @your-org/security-team

# The contribution action used by other repositories. Changing it changes what those repositories send.
/contrib/                   @your-org/network-team @your-org/security-team

# Membership. The bot opens these PRs; the networking team approves. Security is pulled in by the workflow
# only when the file contains an `exceptions:` entry (a raw rule outside the profile catalogue).
/perimeter/members/         @your-org/network-team

# The renderer and the gates. Somebody who can edit these can neutralise every other line in this file.
/terraform/                 @your-org/network-team @your-org/security-team
/policy/                    @your-org/security-team
/tools/                     @your-org/network-team @your-org/security-team
/.github/workflows/         @your-org/network-team @your-org/security-team
